1
00:04:37,142 --> 00:04:43,142
Your mission: don't die.

2
00:09:14,285 --> 00:09:20,285
Doom: Annihilation is a action, science fiction,
horror film directed by Tony Giglio.

3
00:13:51,428 --> 00:13:57,428
A group of UAC Marines responds to a distress call from a top-secret scientific base on
Phobos, a Martian moon, only to discover it's been overrun by demons.

4
00:18:28,571 --> 00:18:34,571
Joan Dark, played by Amy Manson.

5
00:23:05,714 --> 00:23:11,714
Dr. Bennett Stone, played by Luke Allen-Gale.

6
00:27:42,857 --> 00:27:48,857
Carley, played by Nina Bergman.

7
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Dr. Malcolm Betruger, played by Dominic Mafham.

8
00:36:57,142 --> 00:37:03,142
Captain Hector Savage, played by James Weber Brown.

9
00:41:34,285 --> 00:41:40,285
Sandy Peterson, played by Lorina Kamburova.

10
00:46:11,428 --> 00:46:17,428
Doom: Annihilation is a 2019 American science fiction action
film written and directed by Tony Giglio.

11
00:50:48,571 --> 00:50:54,571
It is a reboot based on id Software's Doom franchise and is
the second live-action film after Doom (2005).

12
00:55:25,714 --> 00:55:31,714
The film stars Amy Manson, Dominic Mafham, Luke Allen-Gale, and Nina Bergman.

13
01:00:02,857 --> 01:00:08,857
In the film, marines battle demon-like creatures in a facility on Phobos, who
have emerged from ancient teleportation devices known as "Gates".

14
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:46,000
Giglio pitched his idea for a new film to Universal in
2015, but was initially turned down.

15
01:09:17,142 --> 01:09:23,142
The success of the 2016 video game convinced Universal to
proceed and commission a script from Giglio.

16
01:13:54,285 --> 01:14:00,285
The project was announced in April 2018, with principal photography commencing soon
afterward, and ending in June, with additional photography following in early 2019.

17
01:18:31,428 --> 01:18:37,428
id Software publicly iterated that they were not involved with the film since they
had earlier declined an invitation to participate in its production.

18
01:23:08,571 --> 01:23:14,571
Doom: Annihilation was released direct-to-video on October 1, 2019, to mixed
reviews and earned $78,389 (~$96,407 in 2024) in domestic video sales.

19
01:27:45,714 --> 01:27:51,714
The film explores themes of planet mars, hell,
space, demon, based on video game.

20
01:32:22,857 --> 01:32:28,857
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
